  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find the value of $a$ if:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_1^a\\frac1x\\,dx=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=e^5$",
          "worked": "The integral requires $a>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left[\\ln|x|\\right]_1^a&=5\\\\\\ln a-\\ln1&=5\\\\\\ln a&=5\\\\a&=e^5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_a^e\\frac1x\\,dx=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=e^{-4}$",
          "worked": "The integral requires $a>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left[\\ln|x|\\right]_a^e&=5\\\\\\ln e-\\ln a&=5\\\\1-\\ln a&=5\\\\\\ln a&=-4\\\\a&=e^{-4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_a^{-1}\\frac1x\\,dx=-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-e^2$ (since $a<-1$).",
          "worked": "The integral requires $a<0$ so that its interval does not cross zero.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left[\\ln|x|\\right]_a^{-1}&=-2\\\\\\ln|-1|-\\ln|a|&=-2\\\\-\\ln|a|&=-2\\\\\\ln|a|&=2\\\\|a|&=e^2\\\\a&=-e^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis gives $a<-1$, as required for the negative integral.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_{-e}^a\\frac1x\\,dx=-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-e^{-1}$ (since $a<0$; otherwise the integral is undefined).",
          "worked": "The integral requires $a<0$ so that its interval does not cross zero.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left[\\ln|x|\\right]_{-e}^a&=-2\\\\\\ln|a|-\\ln|-e|&=-2\\\\\\ln|a|-1&=-2\\\\\\ln|a|&=-1\\\\|a|&=e^{-1}\\\\a&=-e^{-1}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
